From 5e308b9182b0915ad12a6b04374af89726219e84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:51:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: every CLI write the stopped Board sync keeps
 local says so; public runstate.when; shared create-note anchors

Follow-up to PR #2033's exact-head review (GitHub review 5888858852, card t_01a1d43d66656ca7): three
non-blocking nits.

1. CLI parity. While this gateway's Board sync is stopped, `kanban archive`, `reopen`, `reopen-review`,
   `request-review`, `request-changes` and `unlink` printed no "Queued locally: ..." notice, though the
   matching tools (kanban_archive, kanban_request_review, ...) return `board_delivery: queued_local`.
   archive and reopen-review now pass `conn=` to `_bulk_apply`; reopen, request-review and request-changes
   print `kanban_board_delivery.cli_lines` through a small `_print_queued_local(conn)`; unlink prints it only
   when a link was actually removed (no write, no notice). `archive --rm` (purge) is left without it.
2. `kanban_board_delivery.queued_local` called the private `kanban_sync_runstate._when`; it is now the
   public `kanban_sync_runstate.when` (no other callers of the old name).
3. `_chat_link_queued` (tools/kanban_tools_board_delivery.py) rewrote the placed kanban_create note with
   `.replace` on literals tools/kanban_tools.py spelled out separately, so rewording the note there made the
   rewrite silently do nothing. Both fragments are now `CHAT_TASKS_SHOWS` / `CHAT_TASKS_QUEUED` in
   kanban_tools_board_delivery, read by kanban_tools at call time when it builds the note.

Proof (tests/tools/test_kanban_board_delivery.py, stopped state from the real SchemaAhead `run_forever`):
- RED at origin/main source with the new tests: 8 failed, 22 passed
  (test_cli_write_while_stopped_prints_the_notice_once[archive|reopen|reopen_review|request_review|
  request_changes|unlink], test_create_note_wording_and_its_stopped_sync_rewrite_share_one_source[created|queued]).
- GREEN: 30 passed. Controls: the same six CLI writes with the sync running print no notice; an unlink of a
  missing link while stopped prints none.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 19 checks ok.
